'output' sections.

32
00:02:41.188 --> 00:02:48.125
NARRATOR: Follow every arrow in order and name
the state before and after each transition.

33
00:02:48.125 --> 00:02:53.719
NARRATOR: The trace converts an abstract
statement into an inspectable sequence.

34
00:02:53.834 --> 00:02:59.998
NARRATOR: Next, compare the choices involved
in Introduction to Programming Language Basics

35
00:02:59.998 --> 00:03:03.080
and make the decision criteria explicit.

36
00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:09.330
NARRATOR: Exceptions interrupt normal control
flow until a matching handler processes them

37
00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:10.893
or they propagate.

38
00:03:10.893 --> 00:03:16.897
NARRATOR: Consider this worked case: Students
will write a Python script that declares

39
00:03:16.897 --> 00:03:23.362
