multiple times in the main program.

74
00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:26.497
NARRATOR: On screen, show a code snippet with
a function definition and two separate calls,

75
00:06:26.497 --> 00:06:28.296
highlighting the reusable block.

76
00:06:28.296 --> 00:06:34.296
NARRATOR: Change one assumption at a time and
observe which part of the reasoning no longer

77
00:06:34.296 --> 00:06:34.671
holds.

78
00:06:34.671 --> 00:06:40.428
NARRATOR: The edge case reveals the boundary
of the claim without discarding the useful

79
00:06:40.428 --> 00:06:41.250
core idea.

80
00:06:41.354 --> 00:06:47.726
NARRATOR: Use Debugging and Testing to
diagnose a failure by separating symptoms,

81
00:06:47.726 --> 00:06:49.850
causes, and corrective action.

82
00:06:49.850 --> 00:06:57.295
NARRATOR: Compiler work separates parsing and
semantic analysis from lowering, verification,

83
00:06:57.295 --> 00:07:00.679
optimization, and target-specific code
generation.

84
00:07:00.679 --> 00:07:06.561
NARRATOR: Consider this worked case: Students
will run a test case with incorrect input,

85
00:07:06.561 --> 00:07:12.444
